            <div xml:id="d89">

                <pb facs="0265" n="177" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg177"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.G/384: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chairman of the
                        American Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hull</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-12-12T20:00:00-05:00">December 12, 1933—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>71. Supplementing Department’s telegram No. 61 of December 9, 4 p.m. Information
                    received today that Nicaragua withdrew from tariff truce effective November
                    30.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
